{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792917823,"nonce":"cpIamvvXDRdhjYRD3jwVYm9xjs0=","title":"TypeScript project cache test sets file times through a read-only handle, refused on Windows","message":"`transitive_and_type_only_edits_recheck_source_and_preserve_diagnostics` (crates/zyntax_ts/tests/project_cache.rs) restores lib.ts's modification time with `File::open(file)?.set_times(...)`. Windows needs FILE_WRITE_ATTRIBUTES on the handle for SetFileTime, which a read-only open does not have, so the call fails with Access is denied (os error 5); Unix accepts it. Seen on x86_64-pc-windows-msvc in Rust CI run 40173953556 (main 5321f901), the first run whose Windows job got past zyntax_embed's tests. The test came in with ee4af47e.","files":null}]}